---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Teleforce"
  description="How Teleforce collects, uses, and shares information from tryteleforce.com and the client portal. Email sales@tryteleforce.com with a request."
>
  <header class="ahead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms</a></div>
      <div class="cat">Legal</div>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="post">
    <p class="lead">How Teleforce handles information from tryteleforce.com and the client portal.</p>
    <p><em>Effective October 24, 2026</em></p>
    <p>
      This policy is from TLF IP LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company operating Teleforce, at
      1111 Brickell Ave, Floor 10, Miami, FL 33131. Questions and privacy requests go to
      <a href="mailto:sales@tryteleforce.com">sales@tryteleforce.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      It covers the public site and the client portal at portal.tryteleforce.com. It is about the
      executive assistant service. It is written in plain language. It is not a substitute for the
      <a href="/terms">Terms</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>We collect what you give us, and a small amount of technical information the site needs to run.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Quiz and site forms.</strong> Work email, and if you continue, name, company, phone, and how you heard about us.</li>
      <li><strong>Signup.</strong> Full name, work email, the password you choose, the plan you select, and that you accepted the Terms. The password is stored as a hash, not as the password itself.</li>
      <li><strong>Payment card.</strong> Entered in Stripe’s secure field. Stripe processes the card. We do not store the full card number. We keep a Stripe customer reference so we can bill the plan when billing starts.</li>
      <li><strong>Booking.</strong> A discovery call uses the Google Calendar scheduler on the site. Onboarding and kickoff use Calendly. Those services collect the name, email, phone, and time you enter there.</li>
      <li><strong>Portal records.</strong> Account details, match status, and, if you accept a match, the time of that acceptance and the browser details sent with the request.</li>
      <li><strong>Cookies and tags.</strong> The site loads a Google Ads tag. It can set cookies and similar identifiers to measure visits and ad conversions. See Cookies below.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Send the quiz plan and reply to a form.</li>
      <li>Create the portal account, schedule onboarding, present a match, and book kickoff.</li>
      <li>Place a card on file and charge it only when the Terms say billing starts.</li>
      <li>Send account, Terms, and match email.</li>
      <li>Measure which ads and pages lead to a quiz submit or a booked call.</li>
      <li>Keep the service secure and meet legal duties.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your information for money.</p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We share information with the companies that run the service. They use it for that purpose.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Stripe</strong> processes the card. We do not store the full card number.</li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong> sends portal email, including the welcome note, the Terms, and match messages.</li>
      <li><strong>FormSubmit</strong> delivers quiz and other site-form submissions to our sales inbox.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> provides the Ads tag and the Calendar appointment scheduler embedded on the site.</li>
      <li><strong>Calendly</strong> provides onboarding and kickoff scheduling at calendly.com/tryteleforce-sales.</li>
      <li><strong>Vercel</strong> hosts the client portal.</li>
      <li><strong>Turso</strong> stores portal account and match records.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We also share information if the law requires it, or if we need to protect Teleforce, our clients, or someone else.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and Google tags</h2>
    <p>
      The site loads Google’s tag for Google Ads (measurement ID AW-18403081564). The tag can store
      cookies or similar identifiers on your browser so we can tell that a visit, a quiz email, or a
      booked call came from an ad. You can block or delete cookies in your browser. If you do, the
      site still works, and ad measurement may be less accurate.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Inquiry and quiz messages stay while we are working the request, and for a reasonable sales
      record after that. Portal account and match records stay for the life of the account, and
      afterward for as long as we need them for billing, security, and legal duties. Card details
      stay with Stripe under Stripe’s own retention rules. You can ask us to delete what we still
      hold. We may keep a limited record of the request itself, and anything we must keep by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Your requests</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:sales@tryteleforce.com">sales@tryteleforce.com</a> to access, correct, or
      delete your information, or to limit how we use it. Tell us the email address you used, and
      what you want. We will reply to that address.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>California.</strong> You can ask us to know, correct, or delete personal information,
      and to opt out of a sale or share. We do not sell personal information for money. The Google
      Ads tag is advertising measurement. If you want that treated as an opt-out of sale or sharing
      under the CCPA, say so in the email and we will honor it for the information we control.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>EEA, UK, and similar laws.</strong> You can ask for access, correction, deletion,
      restriction, a copy, or to object. Email the same address. We are a U.S. company and we do
      not have a representative in the EEA or the UK. You may also complain to your local data
      protection authority.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Teleforce is a business service. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 16.
      If you believe a child gave us information, email
      <a href="mailto:sales@tryteleforce.com">sales@tryteleforce.com</a> and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      When this policy changes, we update this page and the effective date at the top. The new
      version applies from that date. If a change is material, we will also say so on this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Florida</h2>
    <p>
      Teleforce operates from Miami, Florida. Florida residents can use the request rights above,
      and can write us at 1111 Brickell Ave, Floor 10, Miami, FL 33131 or
      <a href="mailto:sales@tryteleforce.com">sales@tryteleforce.com</a>. The
      <a href="/terms">Terms</a> are governed by Florida law. This policy describes how we handle
      information. It does not change those Terms.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .ahead h1 {
    max-width: none;
  }
</style>
